-- title:
--   Verified primality decision by bounded trial division
-- statement:
--   Let $2\le n\le V$ and let $f$ be a scratch base. For machine limits $S,W,D$, assume $f+\lfloor\log_2(V+1)\rfloor+2\le S\le W$, $8V+16\le W$, and $d<D$. Suppose program $P$ contains the primality body and Euclidean-remainder helper. Put $R_V=43(\lfloor\log_2(V+1)\rfloor+1)+34$. From any integer memory $\mu$, execution on $(n,f)$ terminates within $(n-2)(R_V+70)+70$ steps and returns
--
--   $$
--   r=\begin{cases}1&n\text{ is prime},\\0&n\text{ is composite},\end{cases}
--   \qquad \mu'(a)=\mu(a)\quad(a<f).
--   $$
--
--   This supplies a concrete primality test for deterministic prime-pool construction.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/LightPrimality.lean#L97-L156

